# Environment Setup & Dependency Management

## Development Environment

### System Requirements

#### Operating System Support
- **macOS**: 10.15+ (Catalina and later)
- **Linux**: Ubuntu 20.04+, CentOS 8+, Debian 11+
- **Windows**: 10/11 with WSL2 recommended

#### Python Requirements
- **Python Version**: 3.11+ (required)
- **Supported Versions**: 3.11, 3.12
- **Package Manager**: pip 23.0+

#### System Dependencies
```bash
# macOS (via Homebrew)
brew install git python@3.11 pre-commit

# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git python3.11 python3.11-venv python3-pip

# CentOS/RHEL
sudo dnf install git python3.11 python3-pip

# Windows (via Chocolatey)
choco install git python3 --version=3.11.0
```

### Python Environment Management

#### Using pyenv (Recommended)
```bash
# Install pyenv
curl https://pyenv.run | bash

# Install Python 3.11
pyenv install 3.11.0
pyenv global 3.11.0

# Verify installation
python --version  # Should show Python 3.11.0
```

#### Using conda
```bash
# Create conda environment
conda create -n swift-debugging python=3.11
conda activate swift-debugging

# Verify installation
python --version
which python
```

#### Using venv
```bash
# Create virtual environment
python3.11 -m venv venv

# Activate environment
source venv/bin/activate  # Linux/macOS
venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows

# Upgrade pip
pip install --upgrade pip
```

## Project Setup

### Initial Setup
```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/swift-debugging/mcp-server.git
cd mcp-server

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# Install development dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Install pre-commit hooks
pre-commit install

# Verify installation
swift-debugging-mcp-server --version
```

